      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "The cat sat on the mat. A language model reading that sentence assigns probabilities before each next word appears. Evaluation asks how much probability reached the word we actually observed. Perplexity summarizes that predictive fit, giving us a useful comparison when the scoring conditions stay fixed.",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 19.023999999999997,
          "duration": 18.624,
          "until": 19.624
        },
        {
          "say": "Here the words on, the, and mat are three scored targets after the supplied prefix. Treat each displayed word as one token in this constructed example. Their probabilities come from three different prediction steps, each conditioned on the actual preceding words. We score the text rather than sample a continuation.",
          "start": 19.624,
          "end": 39.184,
          "duration": 19.56,
          "until": 39.833999999999996
        },
        {
          "say": "We will turn those probabilities into surprise, combine them into one score, and examine the bookkeeping that makes the result meaningful. The important questions will be which targets were scored, what context they received, and which units sit in the denominator.",
          "start": 39.833999999999996,
          "end": 55.145999999999994,
          "duration": 15.312,
          "until": 55.846
        }
      ],
